      "sourceTextSha256": "aa0ef633f1020f77d87b7c3e4ba7d6c44d6ba4889e5b97ecb4f0cc031cf1ad4f",
      "text": "Day 3 · Corcovado and Christ the Redeemer. After breakfast, your English-speaking guide meets you in the hotel lobby for a 4-hour excursion. An open, eco-friendly train takes you through the lush forest to the summit of Corcovado where, at 710 metres above sea level, stands Rio’s most famous landmark, the 38-metre statue of Christ the Redeemer, erected in 1931, with breathtaking views across the Rio–Niterói Bridge, Guanabara Bay, the Botanical Garden, Maracanã Stadium and Sugar Loaf.",
